WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.267
-Welcome back.
Hey, it is after midnight.

00:00:03.267 --> 00:00:04.434
So I can actually say this.

00:00:04.434 --> 00:00:05.834
Happy birthday, pal!

00:00:05.834 --> 00:00:07.334
It's your birthday!

00:00:07.334 --> 00:00:08.734
-Yeah.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:08.734 --> 00:00:10.000
-Thank you.

00:00:10.000 --> 00:00:12.200
You're the first.
-I'm the very first person.

00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:14.701
-Like, every year.
-Every year.

00:00:14.701 --> 00:00:18.167
-Every year I'm on the show,
and you say it.

00:00:18.167 --> 00:00:21.267
-Yeah. Do you mind me asking,
is it a big birthday?

00:00:21.267 --> 00:00:23.000
-Listen, I was born in the '70s.

00:00:23.000 --> 00:00:25.000
You know, December 8, '79.

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.033
-Wow.

00:00:26.033 --> 00:00:30.167
-And the '70s were crazy,
you know?

00:00:30.167 --> 00:00:34.467
Everybody's pooping their pants
and boobs everywhere.

00:00:34.467 --> 00:00:35.801
You know?
[ Laughter ]

00:00:35.801 --> 00:00:37.067
I mean, every nap I woke up,

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:39.467
just poop in my pants
and boobs in my face.

00:00:39.467 --> 00:00:41.868
I thought, "Oh, yeah,
I think I like it here."

00:00:41.868 --> 00:00:44.133
[ Laughter ]
-Wow.

00:00:44.133 --> 00:00:45.467
-It was a different time,
though.

00:00:45.467 --> 00:00:46.934
The '70s were a different time.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:49.534
-The '70s, yeah. 1979 exactly?

00:00:49.534 --> 00:00:50.400
-Yeah. Yep.

00:00:50.400 --> 00:00:52.033
-Yeah. And then the '80s.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:53.834
-Everyone's learning numbers.

00:00:53.834 --> 00:00:56.234
[ Laughter ]
Yeah.

00:00:56.234 --> 00:00:58.434
Everybody learned how to talk
in the '80s.

00:00:58.434 --> 00:01:00.634
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:03.434
-A wild decade that was.
-Yeah.

00:01:03.434 --> 00:01:05.567
-Do you ever treat yourself
on your birthday?

00:01:05.567 --> 00:01:08.534
-I did this year.
I never do but --

00:01:08.534 --> 00:01:13.734
Listen, I really wanted to know
if I was able to evade the law.

00:01:13.734 --> 00:01:17.534
So I hired a private
investigator to follow myself,

00:01:17.534 --> 00:01:19.901
and I still haven't lost him.

00:01:19.901 --> 00:01:21.801
I've been trying to lose him
a couple days.

00:01:21.801 --> 00:01:24.300
He's good. He's good.

00:01:24.300 --> 00:01:26.133
He doesn't know that
I hired him either.

00:01:26.133 --> 00:01:28.133
So he, like, sends me updates.

00:01:28.133 --> 00:01:31.467
He thinks it's a third party.
So he's like, "Yeah.

00:01:31.467 --> 00:01:34.033
He's at the coffee shop.
He's wearing a weird jacket."

00:01:34.033 --> 00:01:36.534
And I'm like, "I don't know
if it is a weird jacket.

00:01:36.534 --> 00:01:38.567
I mean, it probably looks cool.

00:01:38.567 --> 00:01:41.167
You're probably just not
very good at fashion.

00:01:41.167 --> 00:01:43.934
Stick to the law."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:43.934 --> 00:01:46.033
-How is your son doing?

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.701
-He's great.
-How old is he now?

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.567
-He's eight.
He's eight years old.

00:01:49.567 --> 00:01:51.934
And I mean, he's learning stuff.

00:01:51.934 --> 00:01:53.133
You know?
-He is, yeah.

00:01:53.133 --> 00:01:56.033
-I didn't know it was
going to happen as quick.

00:01:56.033 --> 00:01:58.534
You know, there's things that
you're supposed to teach him,

00:01:58.534 --> 00:02:01.501
but there's also things you
just assume that they know.

00:02:01.501 --> 00:02:03.200
But he got an iPad,

00:02:03.200 --> 00:02:06.300
and I looked on it and didn't
realize there was YouTube on it.

00:02:06.300 --> 00:02:07.701
So I'm like, "Oh, I wonder what
he's watching."

00:02:07.701 --> 00:02:10.133
And I go in. It's mostly
Minecraft videos, you know?

00:02:10.133 --> 00:02:12.734
And also a lot of Nick Thune
videos.

00:02:12.734 --> 00:02:14.801
He's a big fan.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:14.801 --> 00:02:17.901
And I saw one video
that stuck out.

00:02:17.901 --> 00:02:20.701
It was a 30-minute video
of a person

00:02:20.701 --> 00:02:23.434
very calmly explaining
that the Earth is flat.

00:02:23.434 --> 00:02:24.534
[ Laughter ]

00:02:24.534 --> 00:02:26.634
Just the red line to the end.

00:02:26.634 --> 00:02:28.567
He devoured that video.

00:02:28.567 --> 00:02:31.467
And I'm realizing I don't think
I've ever mentioned to him

00:02:31.467 --> 00:02:32.934
that the Earth is round yet.

00:02:32.934 --> 00:02:34.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.934
And could you imagine if
the first thing that you ever

00:02:36.934 --> 00:02:38.167
learn is that it's flat,

00:02:38.167 --> 00:02:39.834
and somebody tells you in
a really convincing way,

00:02:39.834 --> 00:02:43.033
and you look down, and you're
like, "I mean, yeah, obviously.

00:02:43.033 --> 00:02:44.767
Yeah. It's pretty flat."

00:02:44.767 --> 00:02:47.834
So now I'm like, "No, man.
It's round, dude."

00:02:47.834 --> 00:02:49.834
Like, I sound like some hippie
that's like,

00:02:49.834 --> 00:02:53.200
"Yeah, gravity, man.
And I don't get it.

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:54.767
Maybe it is flat. I don't know."
[ Laughter ]

00:02:54.767 --> 00:02:56.400
-Oh, my God, that's a terrible
way to explain.

00:02:56.400 --> 00:02:58.067
-Yeah, I know. I don't know.

00:02:58.067 --> 00:03:01.133
-So Daddy's a round-Earther.

00:03:01.133 --> 00:03:02.767
-Oh, my gosh. Yeah, no, no.

00:03:02.767 --> 00:03:05.701
It is definitely round
if you're watching --

00:03:05.701 --> 00:03:06.801
if your son's watching.
-Yeah.

00:03:06.801 --> 00:03:08.667
[ Laughter ]
-Definitely round.

00:03:08.667 --> 00:03:10.467
You're going back on tour.

00:03:10.467 --> 00:03:12.100
-I am.
-This is exciting.

00:03:12.100 --> 00:03:14.067
The Known European Tour.

00:03:14.067 --> 00:03:15.734
-Yep, I'll be in Europe.

00:03:15.734 --> 00:03:18.534
You know, the E.U. reached out.
They wanted me to come.

00:03:18.534 --> 00:03:20.467
That's the European Union.
-Thank you.

00:03:20.467 --> 00:03:22.801
We went on tour together once.
Do you remember that tour?

00:03:22.801 --> 00:03:24.467
-Do I remember that tour?

00:03:24.467 --> 00:03:25.734
Yeah, it was the highlight
of my life.

00:03:25.734 --> 00:03:27.567
-That was a great tour.

00:03:27.567 --> 00:03:28.801
-It was really fun.

00:03:28.801 --> 00:03:31.067
You brought me
and Nate Bargatze,

00:03:31.067 --> 00:03:33.067
and we all went around,
and Seth was there.

00:03:33.067 --> 00:03:34.334
-Seth Herzog was there.

00:03:34.334 --> 00:03:36.334
I remember I would do
a little bit of stand-up

00:03:36.334 --> 00:03:41.033
and then I would introduce
my favorite comedians.

00:03:41.033 --> 00:03:43.667
We had so much fun.
We went all around the country.

00:03:43.667 --> 00:03:46.734
-I know, and then I remember the
first night you introduced me.

00:03:46.734 --> 00:03:48.667
You said, "Nick Thune."

00:03:48.667 --> 00:03:50.734
And like, I walk out, there's
thousands of people cheering.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.267
-I know exactly what --
-And you go --

00:03:52.267 --> 00:03:53.868
-I know exactly what you did,

00:03:53.868 --> 00:03:55.033
because you did it
more than once.

00:03:55.033 --> 00:03:58.133
-Yeah. But it was, like,
you'd shake my hand --

00:03:58.133 --> 00:04:00.534
-I go, "Here he is, Nick Thune."
I go, "Break a leg man."

00:04:00.534 --> 00:04:03.634
-Yeah, hey, thanks.
By the way, how are you doing?

00:04:03.634 --> 00:04:04.868
-Fine, man.

00:04:04.868 --> 00:04:06.667
-Oh, you know, let's talk about
it after my set.

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.434
-Perfect. Yeah.

00:04:08.434 --> 00:04:10.367
And then I would leave,
but then it got longer.

00:04:10.367 --> 00:04:12.501
-Yeah, I go, "Oh, I was going to
tell you, my mom,

00:04:12.501 --> 00:04:13.968
she's a big fan."

00:04:13.968 --> 00:04:15.801
[ Laughter ]
-Everyone's clapping.

00:04:15.801 --> 00:04:17.567
I go, "Ladies and gentlemen,
Nick Thune."

00:04:17.567 --> 00:04:19.901
Everyone claps. You walk out.
I shake your hand, you're like,

00:04:19.901 --> 00:04:21.901
"Hey, man, do you want to,
like, hang out afterwards?

00:04:21.901 --> 00:04:23.868
And we'll have dinner. Like,
what would you want to eat?

00:04:23.868 --> 00:04:25.300
Like, would you want to eat
Italian food?

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:27.200
Or would you want to have
Chinese food?

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:29.801
Oh, you know what? Never mind.
Let's eat in the hotel room."

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:32.300
-And then I'd pitch you on
some of my business ideas.

00:04:32.300 --> 00:04:33.801
[ Laughter ]

00:04:33.801 --> 00:04:35.934
"Hey, what do you think about
scented Wi-Fi?"

00:04:35.934 --> 00:04:37.634
[ Laughter ]

00:04:37.634 --> 00:04:40.300
"I think we're gonna go big.
I think we're gonna go big."

00:04:40.300 --> 00:04:42.300
-That made me laugh so hard.
I loved it.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:44.300
It got longer and longer
every time I'd introduce you.

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:46.601
I go, "Oh, my gosh,
this guy is amazing."

00:04:46.601 --> 00:04:49.901
I want to talk about also --
You're going on tour.

00:04:49.901 --> 00:04:51.200
Known European Tour.

00:04:51.200 --> 00:04:53.534
But also you're starring in
this film, "Mixtape."

00:04:53.534 --> 00:04:54.667
It's a beautiful movie,
by the way.

00:04:54.667 --> 00:04:56.968
It is funny,
but it's also very touching.

00:04:56.968 --> 00:04:59.234
It's a nice family movie if you
guys want to check it out.

00:04:59.234 --> 00:05:00.567
-You know, I, um...

00:05:00.567 --> 00:05:02.200
No, I'm not going to say it.
I will say it.

00:05:02.200 --> 00:05:03.934
I love you.
[ Audience aws ]

00:05:03.934 --> 00:05:06.667
-You weren't going to say it?
-I wasn't going to say it.

00:05:06.667 --> 00:05:08.234
-Why weren't you going to
say it?

00:05:08.234 --> 00:05:11.534
-Because I was taught
to bury my emotions.

00:05:11.534 --> 00:05:13.000
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:14.267
-Oh, my goodness.

00:05:14.267 --> 00:05:16.167
But now it's your birthday.

00:05:16.167 --> 00:05:17.801
-I'm here.

00:05:17.801 --> 00:05:19.701
-Well, can I just say something
to you?

00:05:19.701 --> 00:05:21.334
-Yeah.
-I love you.

00:05:21.334 --> 00:05:23.601
[ Audience aws ]

00:05:23.601 --> 00:05:25.300
There you go.
-I also love YouTube.

00:05:25.300 --> 00:05:27.534
[ Laughter ]
-Oh, did you say "tube"?

00:05:27.534 --> 00:05:28.601
-Yeah, I was talking about
YouTube.

00:05:28.601 --> 00:05:29.968
-Oh, my God. Sorry about that.

00:05:29.968 --> 00:05:32.067
Yeah, I know, I love YouTube.
-Huge misunderstanding.

00:05:32.067 --> 00:05:34.534
-So sorry, that was weird.

00:05:34.534 --> 00:05:36.200
I want to show everyone a clip.

00:05:36.200 --> 00:05:39.701
Here's Nick Thune in "Mixtape."
Take a look at this.

00:05:39.701 --> 00:05:41.701
-Which song do you want?

00:05:41.701 --> 00:05:43.367
Whichever is the best.

00:05:45.567 --> 00:05:47.567
-Didn't you say
it was a mixtape?

00:05:47.567 --> 00:05:52.501
-It's from a tape of songs
my parents put together?

00:05:52.501 --> 00:05:56.167
-Yeah, then you have listen to
the songs in order, okay?

00:05:56.167 --> 00:06:01.534
A mixtape is a message from the
maker to the listener, right?

00:06:01.534 --> 00:06:05.067
It's not just about which songs,
but in what order.

00:06:05.067 --> 00:06:08.167
Microseconds between segues.
Tempo changes.

00:06:08.167 --> 00:06:10.968
Does it fade out?
Does it fade in?

00:06:10.968 --> 00:06:13.000
Does it matter to you? Okay?

00:06:13.000 --> 00:06:14.634
Alright. Getting nowhere fast.

00:06:14.634 --> 00:06:16.133
Girls that are best.

00:06:17.901 --> 00:06:19.834
Great.

00:06:19.834 --> 00:06:23.634
Hands off and stand there.

00:06:23.634 --> 00:06:25.567
-Message from the maker.

00:06:25.567 --> 00:06:28.234
-Ah! Nick Thune, everybody!

00:06:28.234 --> 00:06:30.634
"Mixtape" is streaming now
on Netflix.

